{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1787155017697,"level":"log","data":["RESULT PARAM =","{\"score\":8,\"level\":\"Mid‑Level Developer\",\"strengths\":[\"Clear, structured explanation of real‑time search implementation using vanilla JS, fetch, and PHP.\",\"Demonstrated awareness of performance optimizations (debouncing, async requests).\",\"Strong emphasis on security (prepared statements, input sanitization).\",\"Comprehensive responsive design strategy (flexbox, grid, media queries, fluid units).\",\"Detailed GitHub Flow workflow with branch naming, CI, PR templates, and code review practices.\",\"Good communication of how market research informs UI/UX decisions.\"],\"weaknesses\":[\"Limited discussion of automated testing (unit, integration, end‑to‑end).\",\"No mention of accessibility (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast).\",\"Lack of detail on error handling and fallback strategies for network failures.\",\"Minimal coverage of code modularity or component architecture (e.g., ES modules, design patterns).\",\"No reference to performance profiling tools (Lighthouse, Web Vitals).\",\"Absence of discussion around documentation or knowledge sharing.\"],\"suggestions\":[\"Add unit tests for JavaScript functions and PHP endpoints (Jest, PHPUnit).\",\"Include accessibility checks (axe, Lighthouse) and describe how you address them.\",\"Explain error handling strategies for fetch failures and server errors.\",\"Show how you structure code into reusable modules or components (ES modules, MVC).\",\"Mention performance monitoring (Web Vitals, Lighthouse audits) and how you act on findings.\",\"Highlight documentation practices (README, inline comments, API docs).\",\"Consider using TypeScript or Flow for type safety in larger projects.\"]}"]}
